(5778644, 839002, 107135, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon and personal best!</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon and personal best!', '2009-12-23 01:22:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5778663, 839729, 108580, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes and comments. There were 4 hired guns at this wedding and at least every other guest had a P&amp;S, bridge or DSLR with them. There were 2 videographers. It was impossible to get a shot without someone having a camera in their hands. If your getting married, insist on only 2 photogs, 1 video and that all other guests will be frisked on the way in.<br/> <br/>Re: Snapshottish? Ok, but why? It was a casual family (of mine) outdoor wedding and not high society papparazzi with all the glitter and gloss of Hollywood.<br/>This was an emotional style impromptu shot and I was asked specifically to get these types of images on the day rather than stuffy, staid, bride smiling at groom or "all the sisters together" now shots.<br/>I saw this coming and prepared myself for the throwing of the flowers by climbing onto a wall. All the other official photog''s were mingling at crowd level getting facials...(pun intended).<br/>As for the flowers, no significance other than they fit the bride''s/maids colour scheme of the day.<br/> <br/>Voters who entered a photo in this challenge gave me: Avg (participants): 4.7500 and yet didn''t bother to comment... 190 of 232 voters gave me 5 or higher and I got some comments, kind and not so kind! Thank you for those!</td>', 'Thanks for the votes and comments. There were 4 hired guns at this wedding and at least every other guest had a P&S, bridge or DSLR with them. There were 2 videographers. It was impossible to get a shot without someone having a camera in their hands. If your getting married, insist on only 2 photogs, 1 video and that all other guests will be frisked on the way in. Re: Snapshottish? Ok, but why? It was a casual family (of mine) outdoor wedding and not high society papparazzi with all the glitter and gloss of Hollywood.This was an emotional style impromptu shot and I was asked specifically to get these types of images on the day rather than stuffy, staid, bride smiling at groom or "all the sisters together" now shots.I saw this coming and prepared myself for the throwing of the flowers by climbing onto a wall. All the other official photog''s were mingling at crowd level getting facials...(pun intended).As for the flowers, no significance other than they fit the bride''s/maids colour scheme of the day. Voters who entered a photo in this challenge gave me: Avg (participants): 4.7500 and yet didn''t bother to comment... 190 of 232 voters gave me 5 or higher and I got some comments, kind and not so kind! Thank you for those!', '2009-12-23 01:37:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5778700, 839770, 32602, '<td valign="top">Fantastic image! Timeless classic.</td>', 'Fantastic image! Timeless classic.', '2009-12-23 02:17:05.000000', NULL, 0),
